{
  "title": "Histiocytoma (Benign Fibrous Histiocytoma)",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pathology/8028/histiocytoma-benign-fibrous-histiocytoma",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 21 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Histiocytomas, also known as benign fibrous histiocytomas, are extremely rare, benign histiocytic lesions of bone. Patients typically present with regional pain and swelling.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with radiographs that show a characteristic lytic lesion with a sclerotic border and biopsy with histology showing spindle cells and foamy macrophages in storiform pattern.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually curettage and bone grafting.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
